  ✓ Stage 4: audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete satisfying witnesses
  ✓ Stage 5: build exhaustive syntax/rule inventory and assess static soundness
  ✓ Stage 6: create and run a fresh false result mutation for non-vacuity
  ✓ Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write the final review
